// surface. Sub-surfaces can be arbitrarily nested and create a tree of
// sub-surfaces. The root surface in a tree of sub-surfaces is the main
// surface. The main surface cannot be a sub-surface, because sub-surfaces
// must always have a parent. A main surface with its sub-surfaces forms a
// (compound) window. For window management purposes, this set of wl_surface
// objects is to be considered as a single window, and it should also behave
// as such. The aim of sub-surfaces is to offload some of the compositing
// work within a window from clients to the compositor. A prime example is a
// video player with decorations and video in separate wl_surface objects.
// This should allow the compositor to pass YUV video buffer processing to
